title What stands between the quoted lines
prompt the standing PETRICHOR lane -- docs-geode, the compressors, the front doors, and the pages a newcomer meets
rota lap 4504, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the threshold page asks what already stands true before anyone argues with it, and the concrete fact here was that nobody had ever run the two selections and looked at what sat between their quoted lines
think my own last lap closed on the strand by name -- a page may quote four lines that all print, in order, and skip a refusal standing between them -- so the lap opened with the measurement rather than with a design
think ran both selected commands whole and read them beside the pages: docs-geode/demos/README.md:91 quotes clutter=43 and fascia=57, which stand adjacent in fascia_metric_v0's output; :110 quotes one met: line and the three closing lines of announced_length_scan, whose output carries six met: lines
think so one pair is an unbroken run and the other has four lines standing inside it, and the guard called both the same thing
think the instrument had to answer contiguity outright rather than by an alignment, since a repeated line makes greedy matching overstate a gap and a gate cannot rest on an overstatement; trying every start position in the real output answers it in one pass with no alignment to choose
think then asked what to gate, and the first answer was wrong: a ceiling on the COUNT of skipped lines would rise every time anybody announces a ladder, since announced_length_scan prints one more met: line per announcement, so that ceiling reds a page nobody touched
obs the shape survives growth where the count does not, so selected_scattered is the ceiling: contiguous today and scattered tomorrow means a line was wedged into the middle of a run a page teaches, which is the fault; scattered today and more scattered tomorrow is the report growing.
obs Built into tools/fixtures/t/tutorial_output_scan.sh as a second reading of each declared selection, after the containment check and inside its exact branch. Two new counts print, selected_contiguous and selected_scattered, beside a SCATTERED_CEILING of 1; the lines standing inside a gathering are named, six of them, so a reader can weigh what a page passes over. Verdict a_selection_broke_its_run, exit 6.
obs Twelve control cases join the pen, 31 to 43, every refusal planted and lifted and the ceiling shown from both sides at 0 and at 1. Two are the design's own load-bearing pair: a line wedged into a contiguous run bites, and a report that grows between two quoted lines goes free with the shape count unmoved.
obs The shape strand is proven load-bearing by mutation -- replacing the contiguity test's failing exit with a success reds seven legs and nothing else.
obs Against myself, and it is this guard's own fault one room over: three headers claimed twenty-nine pen cases while the pen emitted thirty-one the whole time. The number had been read off the witness's assertion list rather than off the control's output, which is exactly a page quoting output nobody ran. Both rosters agree at 43 now, counted by running the control.
obs The demos page itself was sharpened rather than left: its second declaration now says one met line and the three closing lines, gathered from a longer report, so the prose tells a reader it is showing one of six. Nothing structural changed and drift stayed 0.
obs The card cost more than the work did. ITINERARY stood at 40,916 of 40,960, so my account had 922 bytes to live in and the first draft ran 1,232. Seven passes brought it to 40,957 -- three bytes of slack for the next ship, which is a pin telling every lap it is full.
